---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import { SITE } from "../consts";
---
<BaseLayout title="About" description="M. Halsey, mechanical engineer and Maine homeowner. Six years in commercial HVAC controls before installing a cold-climate heat pump in a 1970s house and writing down everything the salespeople skipped.">
  <div class="wrap">
    <article class="post">
      <h1>About</h1>
      <p>My name is {SITE.author}. I am a mechanical engineer who spent six years working on commercial HVAC controls before buying a 1970s house in central Maine in 2021.</p>
      <p>The first winter, the oil furnace died. The second winter, I switched to a cold-climate heat pump. The third winter, I started writing down what I had gotten wrong, because most of it was avoidable and I had paid for the lessons in cold rooms.</p>
      <p>This site is what I wish I had read before signing the install contract. It explains, in plain language, the things HVAC salespeople tend to skip: why your switchover temperature matters more than the brand, why a "15 SEER" sticker can mean two very different things, and why a unit quoted at $14k can land at $22k by the time the truck leaves.</p>
      <p>I do not work for any manufacturer. I take some affiliate commission from retailers when readers buy through links, and I list every one of those relationships on the <a href="/affiliate-disclosure/">disclosure</a> page. I do not accept paid placements or sponsored reviews.</p>
      <p>If you want to write to me, the address is at the bottom of the <a href="/contact/">contact</a> page. I read everything. I sometimes take a while to answer.</p>
    </article>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>